   "body": "## Goal\nReport, do not fix. Prepare POC exit 1 of docs/research/poc/delivery.md (\"Controlled same-version fixtures\") so that it can be executed the moment an owner-authored pair exists: (a) a short plain-language authoring instruction the owner can follow in LabVIEW, (b) a comparison tool that localizes every difference between two VIs of such a pair, (c) a self-check of that tool on controls available today. Expected gain: the decisive open uncertainty (semantic encoding plus integrity/cache dependencies, docs/research/0099-writing-version-effort.md \"What next\") gets a ready, tested measurement instead of an unstaged idea; the next shaper reads `docs/research/poc/pair/selfcheck.json` field `status` and `docs/research/poc/pair/owner-instructions.md`. No session can run LabVIEW: claim no behaviour, no valid edit, no native compatibility. No real pair exists yet; do not fabricate one and do not write any changed VI to disk.\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] `docs/research/poc/pair/owner-instructions.md` (at most 40 lines, short plain sentences, numbered exact steps): the owner creates in one LabVIEW version a minimal VI (two I32 controls wired to Add, one indicator) and saves copies differing by exactly one change each: Add replaced by Subtract with terminals unchanged; one I32 constant 1 changed to 2 in a second minimal VI; each also saved with \"separate compiled code\" enabled; no password. It states file names, what to record (LabVIEW version/bitness, save settings, the exact change) and where to put the files. It notes the originals from delivery.md (add.vi is declared 21.0) and that any single consistent version is acceptable if recorded.\n- [ ] `docs/research/poc/pair/pair_diff.py`: plain python3, takes two VI paths, reuses the pinned loader/inspector already used by docs/research/poc/inspect_vi.py (no new dependency, no download). Output JSON per resource type/ID: present-in-one-only, length, SHA256 of both payloads, and for differing payloads the differing byte ranges (offset, length, both hex, bounded); heap resources (BDHb/FPHb and similar compressed payloads) are compared after decompression as well as raw; BDPW reported per 16-byte chunk; LVSR and vers version fields and VICD/CPC2 presence reported explicitly. It never writes a VI.\n- [ ] `docs/research/poc/pair/selfcheck.json` with `schema_version` 1, `status` (`passed` or `blocked`), `inputs` (paths, SHA256s, pylavi revision 35d2a0318f71dcb87bb9c431dc00700ee6b9fb75), `controls` (array) and `limitations`; a blocked outcome carries a nonempty `blocker`. Controls: identical pair (`$LABVIEW_ENVIRONMENT/pylavi/tests/add.vi` against itself, SHA256 cf4b1f56c8e42a7a353101ba1322aa3d64207bb19df5dc791cb3eedf2bb2f7e8) must yield zero differences; an in-memory single-payload perturbation control (one byte changed in one decompressed heap, held in memory only) must be localized to exactly that resource and offset. Label the perturbation as a tool control, not LabVIEW evidence. On pin mismatch or load failure save the exact blocker and stop.\n- [ ] `docs/research/poc/pair/protocol.md` (at most 60 lines): which questions a real pair can answer (primitive identity span, constant value span, BDPW chunk dependence, LVSR flag and compiled-cache dependence with and without separate compiled code) and which it cannot (general integrity rules, other versions, validity of a future edit, behaviour); how pair hashes and authoring settings are pinned before comparison; the exact replay command.\n- [ ] Change nothing outside `docs/research/poc/pair/`. Existing POC files, verifiers, benchmark pins, product, policy and evaluator files stay unchanged. No corpus scan, no new format research, no repeat of RSRC framing discovery, no owner request file, no git commit. Report what is ready and what the pair must supply.\n## Verification\npython3 -c \"import json,pathlib; p=pathlib.Path('docs/research/poc/pair'); d=json.loads((p/'selfcheck.json').read_text()); assert d['schema_version']==1; assert d['status'] in ('passed','blocked'); assert isinstance(d['controls'],list); assert d['inputs'] and d['limitations']; assert d['status']!='blocked' or d.get('blocker'); assert d['status']!='passed' or len(d['controls'])>=2; assert all((p/n).stat().st_size>0 for n in ('owner-instructions.md','pair_diff.py','protocol.md'))\"\nThis checks committed output structure only; the engine's verification has no prepared sources. Run the actual self-check separately in the session while LABVIEW_ENVIRONMENT is available. A blocked record is preserved evidence, not a passed self-check.\n## Context\n- docs/research/poc/delivery.md, section \"Two concrete exits\", exit 1: read by the shaper; it names the pair, the settings to pin and the spans to compare, and its limits.\n- docs/research/0099-writing-version-effort.md, \"What next\": names this pair as the decisive experiment that is not staged.\n- docs/research/0100-wm1-version-evidence.md: accepted example of pin-checking and raw vers/LVSR extraction with the pinned pylavi; reuse its pattern, not its scope.\n- docs/research/poc/inspect_vi.py and docs/research/poc/README.md section \"Re-encoding and remaining gaps\": existing heap decompression and framing; reuse instead of rediscovering.\n## Budget\nRead docs/research/poc/delivery.md, docs/research/poc/inspect_vi.py, docs/research/poc/edit-readiness.md, the named README section, docs/research/0100-wm1-version-evidence.py, @environment/readiness.json, and bounded excerpts of @environment/pylavi/pylavi/file.py and resource_types.py as directly needed. Parse only @environment/pylavi/tests/add.vi. No whole large JSON files, no history search, no corpus or project enumeration, no downloads. Keep command output short; save selfcheck.json early and report early.\n",
